"tegrates the 604,800-block dispute window.\\n- The workbook's 19,890 FLOP per H100-eq unit is that formula with H100 SXM peak (989,000) standing\\n  in for calibrated `B_p`.\\n- The runtime (#643, specified in #633 as a settlement-exposure bound) computes\\n  `10,000 + 0.01\u00b7B_p\u00b7604,800\u00b71.25`. It uses D-0418's per-G_n/s coefficient as a per-G_n rate, which\\n  counts the window twice and adds surge: 7,560 FLOP per G_n/s, 756,000\u00d7 the ratified requirement.\\n  An 8\u00d7 H200 host at 40% of peak would need 23.9B FLOP. That is more than the 18.47B FLOP issued by\\n  the end of era 6 (genesis 4.40B, block emission 12.11B, developer subsidy 1.96B), so real-hardware\\n  calibration (#2850) cannot be bonded.\\n\\nThe bound was re-derived with today's parameters and the 2026-10 consult's corrections: rewards\\ndivide by credited work, rewards are liquid, and settlement exposure is part of the gain. For emission\\nfraud the floor is `k_min = P\u00b7W/(c\u00b7T)`, with `P\u00b7W` = 43.5M FLOP of miner pot per window in era 0,\\n`c` the effective catch probability and `T` the network credited throughput. The gain never exceeds\\n`P\u00b7W`, so the uncapped linear curve over-deters at the top, and D-0418's no-cap invariant stands.\\n\\n**Decision (proposed):**\\n\\n1. **One unit.** The capacity coefficient is FLOP per G_n/s of **calibrated** cap `B_p`. The exposure\\n   window is inside the coefficient (`k` is sized against gain over the window). The requirement\\n   **MUST NOT** multiply by the revocation or dispute window again.\\n2. **Surge is a separate margin.** `\u03c3 = miner_stake_surge_multiplier_ppm / 10\u2076 \u2265 1` multiplies only the\\n   capacity term:\\n   `required_self_stake(B_p) = min_miner_self_stake + \u03c3\u00b7k\u00b7B_p`.\\n   Whether `\u03c3` applies to every cap or only to provisional/SOFT caps stays with E.33. Until then it\\n   applies to every cap, as the runtime does now.\\n3. **The value of `k` is set at activation, not here.** A later owner decision sets `k`, citing\\n   evidence that it satisfies the security envelope (item 4). The candidate to validate first is\\n   `k = 0.25` FLOP per G_n/s (`VFY/4`) with `\u03c3 = 1.25`. At 40% of peak that is: 1\u00d7 RTX 4090 30,625;\\n   1\u00d7 H100 SXM 133,625; 8\u00d7 H200 999,000; 8\u00d7 B200 2,260,000 FLOP. Analytically it deters liquid,\\n   all-fake emission fraud once credited throughput exceeds about 1.9e8 G_n/s at `c = 0.9`\\n   (7.0e8 at `c = 0.25`). That is a sensitivity result, not a demonstrated bound: `c` is unmeasured,\\n   and enforced detection is dispute-only today.\\n4. **Security envelope and activation gates.** The runtime keeps today's requirement until a value of\\n   `k` is shown to satisfy `c_lower \u00b7 s \u00b7 S_available \u2265 G_max` throughout operation, where:\\n   - `c_lower` is a conservative bound on detection, adjudication **and collection**, not a sampling\\n     rate;\\n   - `G_max` is total retained emission **and settlement** gain, including concurrent and unresolved\\n     exposure, with no collateral counted twice;\\n   - the time until fraudulent crediting stops is bounded, and collateral is retained through\\n     dispute resolution;\\n   - enforcement continues after activation: stale measurements, falling credited throughput or failed\\n     detection liveness block new uncovered exposure, including during bootstrap.\\n\\n   The evidence must also include:\\n   - real-inference calibration (#2850), active or activating in the same upgrade;\\n   - aggregate cap enforcement across a miner's concurrent channels;\\n   - measured detection liveness;\\n   - a reproducible adversarial analysis with runtime tests covering bootstrap, low utilization,\\n     coalitions and capacity exits, with uncertainty margins, where leaving the validated envelope\\n     fails closed.\\n\\n   Activation is a separate owner decision, recorded in Appendix H.\\n5. **Alignment, after ratification and activation:**\\n   - runtime: drop `RevocationLatencyBlocks` from `required_self_stake` and set `CapacityStakePerGflop`;\\n   - `params/` (`miner_capacity_stake_per_gflop`, the revocation and surge descriptions), then\\n     `just verify-params`, the simulator mirror and `check_params.py`;\\n   - the miner-worker bond sizing and faucet sponsor sizing, which mirror the runtime formula and\\n     move with it;\\n   - the Lean `stake_covers_settlement_exposure` statement and the Quint miner-staking spec;\\n   - \u00a76.1, Appendices A and C.1, and the workbook (Projection Input \u00a72), which should use calibrated\\n     `B_p` instead of peak spec;\\n   - the published surfaces that quote 7,560 FLOP per G_n/s: the knowledge pages, the intro and\\n     params pages, the onboarding docs and the runbooks.\\n\\n**Rejected:**\\n\\n- *Keep the runtime formula.* Hardware-scale caps cannot be bonded.\\n- *Keep `k = 0.01`.* It deters only above about 4.8e9 G_n/s credited at `c = 0.9`.\\n- *Ratify `k = 0.25` now.* Bondability and conditional thresholds do not establish deterrence while\\n  `c` is unmeasured (2026-10 consult).\\n- *Settlement-exposure sizing (cap \u00d7 window \u00d7 price per G_n).* The model-registry base price\\n  (0.003 FLOP/G_n) is devnet-scale: at that price a week of 8\u00d7 H200 service bills about 5.7B FLOP. It\\n  needs its own recalibration, and settlement exposure is bounded by escrow and aggregate cap\\n  enforcement, not by this bond.\\n- *A cap or sublinear curve.* Unnecessary, since the gain is bounded by `P\u00b7W`, and D-0418 rejects it.\\n\\n**Owner decision requested:**\\n\\n1. Ratify the unit and window placement now (items 1\u20132).\\n2. Adopt `k = 0.25` as the candidate to validate, or name another; 0.05 and 1.0 are tabulated in the\\n   analysis.\\n3. Approve the security envelope and gates (item 4), which fund the adversarial analysis that sets\\n   `k`.\\n\\n**Specification:** \u00a76.1, Appendices A, C.1, E.33, H; `params/flop-protocol-params.yaml`\\n(`miner_capacity_stake_per_gflop`, `miner_stake_revocation_latency_blocks`,\\n`miner_stake_surge_multiplier_ppm`); analysis.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## D-0533 \u2014 Model-registry base price per G_n: a reference set against emission at a reference throughput\\n\\n**Status:** proposal pending ratification (follow-up to #1361 and D-0532). Nothing changes in the\\nruntime, `params/` or published surfaces until the owner ratifies the method and a later decision\\nsets the value at activation.\\n\\n**Context.** `ModelRegistryBasePricePerGFLOP` = 0.003 FLOP per `G_n` was sized for devnet throughput\\n(about 1e3 `G_n/s` network-wide). Its only stated derivation is a simulator input denominated in USD\\nper GFLOP (analysis).\\n\\nReal-inference calibration (#2850) puts caps near 1e5\u20131e7 `G_n/s` per host. At 0.003, one 8\u00d7 H200\\nhost at 40% of peak bills about 9,500 FLOP/s. That is 132\u00d7 the whole era-0 miner pot, or 5.74B FLOP\\nper week against 18.47B FLOP issued by the end of era 6.\\n\\nThe price does four jobs today:\\n- it is the gateway's de facto bill: gateway escrow is estimated `G_n` \u00d7 epoch price, and a\\n  cooperative settle pays the whole escrow;\\n- it sets the `certificate_settle` floor;\\n- it is every new model's default price;\\n- base/10 floors publisher overrides.\\n\\nThe market factor is inert: `Permill::from_percent(200)` saturates at 100%, so the epoch price\\nalways equals the model's price.\\n\\n**Decision (proposed):**\\n\\n1. **Method (to ratify).** The base price is a FLOP-denominated reference, not a peg:\\n   `p_ref = \u03c6 \u00b7 P_m(e) / T_ref`. It is the era-`e` miner emission per credited `G_n` at a reference\\n   network throughput `T_ref`, scaled by `\u03c6`, the ratio of gross fees to the miner emission pot.\\n   - No exchange rate enters.\\n   - The emission rate is the design reference D-0532 uses. Channel payouts do not earn it today\\n     (E.44).\\n2. **Benchmark (to validate, not ratified).**\\n   - The inputs are `\u03c6 = 1` and `T_ref` = 500 H100-equivalent units (the workbook's testnet T3 basis)\\n     \u00d7 740,140 `G_n/s` \u00d7 40% = 1.48e8 `G_n/s`.\\n   - That gives 4.86e-7, so the benchmark is **5e-7 FLOP per `G_n`** (`VFY / 2_000_000`,\\n     500,000,000,000 base units).\\n   - `T_ref` is a scenario, not measured throughput. The parity price scales as `1/u` (1.95e-6 at\\n     10% utilization). On a PCIe-equivalent unit instead of the measured SXM unit, it is about\\n     6.4e-7.\\n   - At 5e-7: a 70B-class 1k-token request costs 0.07 FLOP, an 8\u00d7 H200 host-week bills 0.96M FLOP,\\n     and the publisher floor is 5e-8.\\n3. **Bounds on `\u03c6` (analysis, not ratified).** Let `m` be the miner share of a settlement payment:\\n   0.85 under ratified D-0525, 0.99 in today's runtime.\\n   - **Bond.** If D-0532's envelope counts settlement gain at `p_ref`, the bond must cover\\n     `(1 + m\u03c6)\u00b7k_min(T_ref)`. Holding that to 1.0 FLOP per `G_n/s` at `c = 0.9` gives\\n     `\u03c6 \u2264 ~2`.\\n   - **Wash demand.** Fee leakage deters it only at `\u03c6 \u2265 1/(1\u2212m)` (6.7 to 100), and only if credit\\n     checked the price paid, which it does not. The base price makes no claim against wash demand;\\n     that stays with E.49.\\n4. **Activation (a separate owner decision).** The activated value cites:\\n   - measured eligible credited throughput (indexer realized index, settled `G_n`) and #2850 caps;\\n   - the reward and fee split live at activation (E.44 credit, D-0525 `m`);\\n   - migration of existing `avg` and epoch prices, outstanding gateway quotes and open certificate\\n     channels;\\n   - minimum-escrow, existential-deposit and rounding boundaries;\\n   - audit funding at measured claim frequency and cost.\\n\\n   The value is revisited at each halving (`\u03c6` doubles at constant throughput), or when realized\\n   credited throughput leaves `[T_ref/10, 10\u00b7T_ref]`.\\n5. **D-0532 coupling.**\\n   - Settlement exposure stays bounded by escrow and aggregate cap enforcement, as D-0532 states.\\n   - The adversarial analysis that sets D-0532's `k` adds a settlement term: `m \u00d7 (escrow a miner can\\n     collect in W)`. That counts gateway estimates, publisher prices above `p_ref`, and contract\\n     prices. At exactly `p_ref` it equals `m\u00b7\u03c6\u00b7k_min(T_ref)` per `G_n/s` (0.29\u20130.33 at the benchmark,\\n     `c = 0.9`), and it does not fall as throughput grows.\\n   - The base-price change and D-0532 activation ship in the same upgrade or in a fixed order.\\n     Otherwise hardware-scale caps would meet a 0.003 gateway bill.\\n6. **Coupled items (each a separate owner decision):**\\n   - `rate_G` and `channel_base_per_turn` (E.24), today 1e-18 FLOP per `G_n`, with `p_ref` as the\\n     natural reference;\\n   - audit funding (earmark, `audit_fee_per_turn`, claim frequency), which must stay solvent without\\n     lowering `c`;\\n   - the simulator mirror, which becomes a FLOP-denominated input.\\n7. **Alignment, after activation:**\\n   - the runtime constant and `param_consts.rs`;\\n   - `#[pallet::constant]` exposure;\\n   - the market-factor unit fix (or removal of `MaxMarketFactorPercent`);\\n   - promotion into `params/flop-protocol-params.yaml` with a `check_params.py` entry, then\\n     `just verify-params`;\\n   - a reset of every registered model's `avg` and epoch price;\\n   - the docs that quote 0.003.\\n\\n**Rejected:**\\n\\n- *Keep 0.003.* One host bills 132\u00d7 the miner pot, a single 70B-class request exceeds\\n  `agent_per_tx_limit`, and the base/10 floor blocks hardware-scale publisher prices.\\n- *Halve the base with emission.* Pegs fees to the subsidy.\\n- *Size from the bond (`k/(W\u00b7\u03c3)`).* Makes the bond the price oracle.\\n- *Tier multipliers per `G_n`.* `G_n` per token already scales with model size.\\n- *Ratify 5e-7 now.* `T_ref` is a scenario, and both channel reward credit and the D-0525 split are\\n  unimplemented (2026-10 consult).\\n- *Price high enough to deter wash.* Unbondable under D-0532, and ineffective without a price gate on\\n  credit.\\n\\n**Owner decision requested:**\\n\\n1. Ratify the method (item 1).\\n2. Adopt 5e-7 FLOP per `G_n` as the benchmark to validate, or name another `\u03c6`, `T_ref` or\\n   utilization.\\n3. Approve the activation evidence, the D-0532 coupling and the activation order (items 4\u20135).\\n\\n**Specification:** \u00a712.1 R12.1d, Appendices A, E.24, E.44, E.49; `pallets/runtime/zkverify/src/lib.rs`\\n(`ModelRegistryBasePricePerGFLOP`, `ModelRegistryMaxMarketFactorPercent`); `params/system-settings.yaml`;\\nanalysis.\\n\",\"lastModified\":null},{\"source\":\"https://registry.npmjs.org/@flop-labs/client\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:29.646Z\",\"body\":\"{\\\"_id\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/client\\\",\\\"_rev\\\":\\\"3-8fc1ee73ef32bd6a76d0121cb2134aa8\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/client\\\",\\\"dist-tags\\\":{\\\"latest\\\":\\\"0.2.1\\\"},\\\"versions\\\":{\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/client\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/client@0.0.0-stage\\\",\\\"stub\\\":true,\\\"maintainers\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"}],\\\"dist\\\":{\\\"shasum\\\":\\\"e763e555f50a6130052d5e21296066079bebd01d\\\",\\\"tarball\\\":\\\"https://registry.npmjs.org/@flop-labs/client/-/client-0.0.0-stage.tgz\\\",\\\"fileCount\\\":2,\\\"integrity\\\":\\\"sha512-Lm9YwIrHWvnkf/pSP+tKdWN1vWE0z1ygYqE9SdSkJ2HcSlDkzHOevWB91OnB9hHhKuPsRUcUHa1Ytyv6nPLCsw==\\\",\\\"signatures\\\":[{\\\"sig\\\":\\\"MEYCIQDBBKWlRYtNrUtXeMWwLXOob682EJEK18rJ79Xixmar/gIhAPbWsMBF0lnO4SJYC7tqeNTb3ED1/UArzLvYqrmlCz+I\\\",\\\"keyid\\\":\\\"SHA256:DhQ8wR5APBvFHLF/+Tc+AYvPOdTpcIDqOhxsBHRwC7U\\\"}],\\\"unpackedSize\\\":339},\\\"_npmUser\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Temporary package placeholder for staged publishing\\\",\\\"directories\\\":{},\\\"deprecated\\\":\\\"Staged-publishing placeholder, not a release. Install the latest version.\\\"},\\\"0.2.1\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/client\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"0.2.1\\\",\\\"license\\\":\\\"MIT OR Apache-2.0\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/client@0.2.1\\\",\\\"maintainers\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"}],\\\"homepage\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core#readme\\\",\\\"bugs\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core/issues\\\"},\\\"dist\\\":{\\\"shasum\\\":\\\"86c5c476a34f3088c74eb920c0df39914204b2d4\\\",\\\"tarball\\\":\\\"https://registry.npmjs.org/@flop-labs/client/-/client-0.2.1.tgz\\\",\\\"fileCount\\\":20,\\\"integrity\\\":\\\"sha512-bEss+3+ABiR1iCW1QF2zVUdkrlwBMPTbYhvIiimiGf0ft6U13/6i2Q4FMIsodl0J+OZRMdPM3y3cKantuvP1uw==\\\",\\\"signatures\\\":[{\\\"sig\\\":\\\"MEUCIAYdZIBr3V+zZdmTXNkdEv03Vzwa38cuUVZyXG0M979sAiEAh07NbRfmYh8LpWIIttUwqIPF5GYO0AlwiqkiCCLVRAM=\\\",\\\"keyid\\\":\\\"SHA256:DhQ8wR5APBvFHLF/+Tc+AYvPOdTpcIDqOhxsBHRwC7U\\\"},{\\\"sig\\\":\\\"MEYCIQDatowgsm6fLDqcHsBsb/T9/l0BKpbFetXv5rf8GrnTLgIhAOmk5xcCbITbx3ENWeEcSElp+V1okXmgM8/AU3wGtBDJ\\\",\\\"keyid\\\":\\\"SHA256:DhQ8wR5APBvFHLF/+Tc+AYvPOdTpcIDqOhxsBHRwC7U\\\"}],\\\"unpackedSize\\\":76392},\\\"main\\\":\\\"./dist/index.js\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"module\\\",\\\"_from\\\":\\\"file:tarballs/flop-labs-client-0.2.1.tgz\\\",\\\"types\\\":\\\"./dist/index.d.ts\\\",\\\"engines\\\":{\\\"node\\\":\\\">=22\\\"},\\\"exports\\\":{\\\".\\\":{\\\"types\\\":\\\"./dist/index.d.ts\\\",\\\"import\\\":\\\"./dist/index.js\\\"}},\\\"scripts\\\":{\\\"test\\\":\\\"pnpm test:types && node --import tsx --test tests/*.test.ts\\\",\\\"build\\\":\\\"tsc\\\",\\\"test:types\\\":\\\"tsc -p tsconfig.type-tests.json\\\"},\\\"_npmUser\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"},\\\"_resolved\\\":\\\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-svidyuk-me-flop-core--claude-worktrees-issue-grooming-triage-cd2a2a/e6f8f9ef-a4b2-4f41-95d7-9737f3556783/scratchpad/npm-bootstrap/tarballs/flop-labs-client-0.2.1.tgz\\\",\\\"_integrity\\\":\\\"sha512-bEss+3+ABiR1iCW1QF2zVUdkrlwBMPTbYhvIiimiGf0ft6U13/6i2Q4FMIsodl0J+OZRMdPM3y3cKantuvP1uw==\\\",\\\"repository\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"git+https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core.git\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"git\\\",\\\"directory\\\":\\\"sdk/client\\\"},\\\"_npmVersion\\\":\\\"11.15.0\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Fetch client for FLOP public model discovery and gateway chat completions\\\",\\\"directories\\\":{},\\\"sideEffects\\\":false,\\\"_nodeVersion\\\":\\\"24.16.0\\\",\\\"dependencies\\\":{\\\"@flop-labs/contracts\\\":\\\"^0.1.1\\\"},\\\"publishConfig\\\":{\\\"access\\\":\\\"public\\\"},\\\"_hasShrinkwrap\\\":false,\\\"devDependencies\\\":{\\\"tsx\\\":\\\"^4.23.15\\\",\\\"typescript\\\":\\\"^7.0.2\\\",\\\"@types/node\\\":\\\"^26.6.2\\\"},\\\"_npmOperationalInternal\\\":{\\\"tmp\\\":\\\"tmp/client_0.2.1_1793246504709_0.5034909483954365\\\",\\\"host\\\":\\\"s3://npm-registry-packages-npm-production\\\"}}},\\\"time\\\":{\\\"created\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T04:00:48.967Z\\\",\\\"modified\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T05:12:09.241Z\\\",\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T04:00:48.967Z\\\",\\\"0.2.1\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T04:01:44.835Z\\\"},\\\"bugs\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core/issues\\\"},\\\"license\\\":\\\"MIT OR Apache-2.0\\\",\\\"homepage\\\":\\\"https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core#readme\\\",\\\"repository\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"git+https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core.git\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"git\\\",\\\"directory\\\":\\\"sdk/client\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Fetch client for FLOP public model discovery and gateway chat completions\\\",\\\"maintainers\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"}],\\\"readme\\\":\\\"# @flop-labs/client\\\\n\\\\nA small ESM Fetch client for FLOP's public gateway, for browsers and Node.js 22 or later. Its only runtime dependency is `@flop-labs/contracts`.\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\npnpm add @flop-labs/client\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\nimport { FlopClient, FlopHTTPError } from \\\\\\\"@flop-labs/client\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\nconst client = new FlopClient({ apiKey: \\\\\\\"your-flop-api-key\\\\\\\" });\\\\nconst models = await client.listModels();\\\\nconst model = await client.getModel(models.data[0].id);\\\\n\\\\ntry {\\\\n  const completion = await client.createChatCompletion({\\\\n    model: model.data.id,\\\\n    messages: [{ role: \\\\\\\"user\\\\\\\", content: \\\\\\\"Hello\\\\\\\" }],\\\\n    stream: false,\\\\n  }, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000) });\\\\n  console.log(completion.choices);\\\\n} catch (error) {\\\\n  if (error instanceof FlopHTTPError) {\\\\n    console.log(error.status, error.retryAfter);\\\\n    // error.body retains the gateway's structured error, or non-JSON text.\\\\n  }\\\\n  throw error;\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe default `baseURL` is `https://api.flop.network/v1`, the public alias documented in [`services/rest-gateway/README.md`](https://github.com/flop-labs/flop-core/blob/main/services/rest-gateway/README.md). An origin-only URL gets `/v1` appended. An explicit API path must end in `/v1` (including `/api/v1`); trailing slashes are removed. HTTP(S) URLs with credentials, queries, or fragments are rejected. Redirects are never followed; browsers may expose them as an opaque HTTP error with status 0.\\\\n\\\\nModel discovery needs no API key and sends no bearer credential. Chat completions require `apiKey` and send it only to the configured gateway. Keep privileged credentials on a server. `fetch` can be injected for tests or a compatible transport. Each method accepts an optional caller `signal`. Requests use `credentials: \\\\\\\"omit\\\\\\\"` and `redirect: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"`.\\\\n\\\\nRequests are validated before network access; successful JSON responses are checked structurally using the shared contracts. Provider extensions and receipt fields are returned unchanged. These are **gateway-reported data**: the client does not verify receipts, attestations, payments, chain inclusion, or finality.\\\\n\\\\nVersion 0.1 supports `listModels()`, `getModel(id)`, `createChatCompletion(request)` (JSON), and `streamChatCompletion(request)` (SSE). Wallet operations, x402 funding, and grant minting are outside this surface. Paid requests are sent once: there are no automatic retries, including on 429, cancellation, or transport failure. A timeout does not establish that the gateway did no work; resolve that outcome before manually repeating a paid call.\\\\n\\\\n`listModels` also accepts `offset` (a non-negative integer), `limit` (1\u20131000), `output_modalities` and `supported_parameters` (arrays of names), alongside `signal`. These serialize to the public model feed's query parameters; model detail ids are encoded as one path segment.\\\\n\\\\n`FlopHTTPError` retains `status`, `body`, and the raw `retryAfter` header. Its message excludes request credentials and gateway body content. `FlopValidationError` reports malformed configuration, input, or successful responses. `FlopTransportError` preserves the underlying transport failure as `cause`; caller cancellation propagates the signal's reason. Avoid logging error bodies or causes without applying your application's data policy.\\\\n\\\\n## Streaming chat completions\\\\n\\\\n`streamChatCompletion` returns an async generator. It dispatches one POST when first\\\\niterated, forces `stream: true`, and rejects an explicit `stream: false`. It yields\\\\nstructurally validated `ChatCompletionChunk` objects and returns a\\\\n`ChatCompletionStreamResult` on successful termination. Use `next()` to retain that\\\\nterminal return value (`for await` consumes chunks but discards the return value):\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\nconst stream = client.streamChatCompletion({\\\\n  model: \\\\\\\"flop/model\\\\\\\",\\\\n  messages: [{ role: \\\\\\\"user\\\\\\\", content: \\\\\\\"Hello\\\\\\\" }],\\\\n}, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30_000) });\\\\n\\\\nwhile (true) {\\\\n  const next = await stream.next();\\\\n  if (next.done) {\\\\n    console.log(next.value.finishReason, next.value.usage, next.value.receipt);\\\\n    console.log(next.value.toolCalls); // Complete calls assembled by index.\\\\n    break;\\\\n  }\\\\n  console.log(next.value.choices[0]?.delta.content ?? \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\");\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe iterator enforces the role/content/tools/finish/usage/`[DONE]` lifecycle.\\\\nOnly a valid success\\\\nfinish, usage/receipt frame, `[DONE]`, and a closed body produce a terminal result.\\\\nNo result is returned on early iterator closure; closing it cancels the body\\\\nreader. The client reads through EOF to reject data frames after `[DONE]`.\\\\n\\\\nBefore a stream opens, non-success HTTP statuses throw `FlopHTTPError`, retaining\\\\nthe body and `Retry-After`. HTTP 200 requires `text/event-stream`; a JSON replay\\\\nresponse to a streaming request is rejected. In-band failures throw `FlopStreamError`\\\\nwith `body`, `usageSource` (`\\\\\\\"estimated\\\\\\\"` when supplied), `retryAfter` (seconds), and\\\\n`outputStreamed`. Receipt usage and estimated error usage remain distinct.\\\\nMalformed frames or ordering throw `FlopValidationError`. Missing `[DONE]` or a\\\\ntransport failure throws `FlopStreamInterruptionError`, with the cause when known.\\\\n\\\\nAborting rejects with the signal's exact reason and cancels the reader. Cancellation\\\\nstops reading; it does not undo accepted work or payment. No error or interruption\\\\ntriggers a retry. Reconciliation and any replay are the caller's decision.\\\\n\\\\n## Caller-owned replay identity\\\\n\\\\nBoth paid methods accept `{ idempotencyKey }` alongside `signal`. The key is sent as\\\\n`Idempotency-Key`, must contain 1\u2013128 printable ASCII characters without whitespace,\\\\nand is rejected on discovery GETs. The client never creates a key or retries for you.\\\\nFor durable recovery use `createChatCompletion` with `stream: false`: the gateway\\\\nstores a completed JSON response for replay, rather than a replayable SSE body.\\\\n\\\\n## Task correlation\\\\n\\\\nThe gateway groups an agent task's turns by `X-Correlation-ID`. Call `client.task()` once\\\\nper task and make that task's paid calls through the returned handle: each call sends the\\\\nsame random id, and the next `task()` call starts a new one.\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\nconst task = client.task(); // or client.task(\\\\\\\"job-42\\\\\\\") to supply your own id\\\\nawait task.createChatCompletion({ model: \\\\\\\"qwen/qwen3-8b\\\\\\\", messages });\\\\nawait task.createChatCompletion({ model: \\\\\\\"qwen/qwen3-8b\\\\\\\", messages: [...messages, reply, toolResult] });\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nEither method also accepts `{ correlationId }` directly. The value follows the\\\\nidempotency-key token rules and is rejected on discovery GETs. Do not reuse one id across\\\\ntasks, because the gateway would merge them into one session. A replay under an\\\\nidempotency key must send its original correlation id.\\\\n\\\",\\\"readmeFilename\\\":\\\"README.md\\\"}\",\"lastModified\":\"Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:12:10 GMT\"},{\"source\":\"https://registry.npmjs.org/@flop-labs/contracts\",\"status\":200,\"measuredAt\":\"2026-11-06T03:27:30.263Z\",\"body\":\"{\\\"_id\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/contracts\\\",\\\"_rev\\\":\\\"3-ae661e23efe580343e54f41986ad85aa\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/contracts\\\",\\\"dist-tags\\\":{\\\"latest\\\":\\\"0.1.1\\\"},\\\"versions\\\":{\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/contracts\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"0.0.0-stage\\\",\\\"_id\\\":\\\"@flop-labs/contracts@0.0.0-stage\\\",\\\"stub\\\":true,\\\"maintainers\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"svidyuk\\\",\\\"email\\\":\\\"svidyuk@gmail.com\\\"}],\\\"dist\\\":{\\\"shasum\\\":\\\"769b4b16f95d16cc963abf041afc4876b863090f\\\",\\\"tarball\\\":\\\"https://registry.npmjs.org/@flop-labs/contracts/-/contracts-0.0.0-stage.tgz\\\",\\\"fileCount\\\":2,\\\"integrity\\\":\\\"sha512-T0KRUNpmz8FsT554NsRrDYdDUOIcPhF9cw1m5pHQI6p3z6KhEq/0Tnk7DCA/ooX+0rmwB24OGynjl9iZox